# Scheduling: optimize the hot update loop nest.
#
# We tile and unroll the inner j loop of the update phase. This:
#   * Improves spatial locality for C[i, j] within each tile.
#   * Exposes straight-line code to the backend compiler after
#     unrolling, which typically results in better instruction-level
#     parallelism and easier auto-vectorization.
#   * Preserves the triangular iteration space via guarded iterations.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------

# Start from the baseline kernel.
p0 = kernel_syr2k_unoptimized

# Locate the second j-loop (the one in the update phase). The first
# j-loop scales C; the second performs the rank-2k update and dominates
# the run time, so we only tile that one.
update_j = p0.find_loop("j #1")

# Tile the j loop by a factor of 32.
# tail="guard" keeps a single tiled loop and injects bounds checks
# inside the tile so that we still exactly cover j in [0, i].
